  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_03. Let quadrilateral ABCD be a 4-sided figure with AB = 5, BC = 7, CD = 6, DA = 8. Let quadrilateral EFGH be a 4-sided figure. ABCD is dilated to form EFGH with scale factor 0.5, centered at point O. Find the length of FG in EFGH.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A graphic designer is working on a scaled-down blueprint of a quadrilateral floor plan ABCD for a small apartment. The original design has sides measuring AB = 5 meters, BC = 7 meters, CD = 6 meters, and DA = 8 meters. To fit the plan on a standard sheet of paper, she reduces the design using a dilation centered at point O with a scale factor of 0.5.\n\nThis creates the smaller blueprint EFGH, where each side of the new figure is half the length of the corresponding side in the original plan.\n\nWhen the designer measures the blueprint to order materials for the actual apartment, she needs to know the length of side FG on the scaled drawing. What is the length of FG?"
}